//@version=6
// =============================================================================
// BASIC BREAKS  —  v2, rebuilt from scratch against the worked example
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE BUY SIDE (mirror it for sells)
//
//   Price declines. On the way down it leaves a run of LOWER HIGHS behind it.
//   Those are the levels — a strictly descending run. A high that a later,
//   higher high supersedes leaves the pool; it was never a lower high in that
//   run. Price then rallies and takes them back, NEWEST-MADE FIRST:
//
//       the LAST high made        →  1st Break
//       the one before it         →  2nd Break
//       the one before that       →  3rd Break        … and so on.
//
//   Worked example, GC1! 1h, the decline into 14 Aug 04:00 — six levels at
//   4498 / 4487 / 4458 / 4443 / 4431 / 4419, made in that order. The rally
//   numbers them 1st 4419, 2nd 4431, 3rd 4443, 4th 4458, 5th 4487, 6th 4498.
//
//   THE SET CLOSES ON THE 1st BREAK. The moment price closes above the nearest
//   level, the set is fixed as it stands. Highs the rally makes on its own way
//   up cannot join it — they belong to the next leg.
//
//   The count is UNCAPPED. Only the first three are DRAWN by default; the rest
//   are counted and can be switched on.
//
//   A break is a CLOSE beyond the level. A wick through that closes back inside
//   is a fake-out and breaks nothing.
//
// WHAT COUNTS AS A LEVEL — BODIES, NOT WICKS
//
//   A wick on its own is not a high and closing through one is not a break. A
//   level sits on the CANDLE BODY: the top of a body is max(open, close), the
//   bottom is min(open, close). A spike whose body never reached up there is not
//   a level at all. Reading levels off wick extremes is what put a phantom
//   break on the chart and pushed every real number one slot along.
//
//   A turn also needs AT LEAST TWO OPPOSING CANDLES — at a high, a bullish
//   candle handing over to a bearish one; at a low, a bearish handing over to a
//   bullish. More than two is fine, two is the minimum, one is never enough.
//   The level is the body extreme of that pair, and the pair has to top (or
//   bottom) the bars either side of it.
//
//   The sequence is abandoned if price closes back below the low the rally came
//   off — that setup is done. The levels still in it were never broken, so they
//   go BACK into the pool for the next attempt.
//
// Non-repainting: a turn is only CONFIRMED once the bars to its right have
// closed, and a break is judged once, at bar close.
//
// THE ENTRY sits on the Nth break — the 2nd by default. The signal is made the
// moment that candle CLOSES; the marker is drawn on the NEXT candle, which is
// the one actually taken.
//
// THE ZONE is drawn at the 1st Break. Demand runs from that level down to the
// low the rally came off, with the 50% marked through the middle. Supply is the
// mirror. A zone is RETIRED the moment price closes through the far edge, and
// only the last N live ones stay on the chart.
// =============================================================================
indicator("Basic Breaks", "BREAKS", overlay = true, max_bars_back = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 100)

// ===================== STRUCTURE =============================================
gS = "Structure"
pvLen = input.int(1, "Bars clear either side of a turn", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = gS, tooltip = "A turn is two opposing candles — a bullish handing over to a bearish at a high, the mirror at a low. This is how many bars either side of that PAIR have to stay inside it for the turn to count.\n\n1 (default) — the minimum, so a two-candle turn counts. Every turning point matters no matter how small; on the worked example the levels at 4431, 4443 and 4459 sit in two- and three-candle turns and anything higher loses them.\n\nRaise it only if it is picking up turns you would not count."
buyOn = input.bool(true, "Buy side  —  highs of a decline, broken upward", group = gS)
sellOn = input.bool(false, "Sell side  —  lows of a rally, broken downward", group = gS, tooltip = "OFF by default. This is the mirror image: the lows a rally leaves behind, taken back downward, for sell setups. Reading buy setups off a decline, it is nothing but clutter running down the leg.")
minGap = input.float(0.8, "Levels closer than (× ATR) are the same level", minval = 0.0, maxval = 5.0, step = 0.1, group = gS, tooltip = "A small corner inside a leg is a genuine lower high, so no structural rule removes it — but it takes a number that belongs to the real level above it, which is what puts a wrong 4th on the chart.\n\nWhen a new high lands within this distance of the one already on top, the NEWER, lower one supersedes it rather than sitting beside it.\n\n0.8 is a narrow window: on the worked example 0.8 drops the stray corner and keeps all six real levels, while 1.0 starts eating the 4th. Set to 0 to keep every corner.")
poolMax = input.int(60, "Track at most N levels per side", minval = 3, maxval = 300, group = gS, tooltip = "Bounds the level pool. The OLDEST is dropped when full, and in a decline the oldest is the highest — so if a deep move stops being numbered part-way, raise this.")

// ===================== WHAT GETS DRAWN =======================================
gD = "What gets drawn"
showAll = input.bool(false, "Draw every break", group = gD, tooltip = "Off by default: only the first three of each sequence are drawn. The 4th, 5th, 6th are still COUNTED — they just are not put on the chart. Turn this on to see all of them.")
showN = input.int(3, "…otherwise draw only the first N", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = gD)
histBars = input.int(400, "Only annotate the last N bars  (0 = all)", minval = 0, maxval = 5000, group = gD, tooltip = "Clears older marks off the chart so only the price action you are looking at is annotated.")
c1 = input.color(#5B9CF6, "1st", inline = "c", group = gD)
c2 = input.color(#0C9EC4, "2nd", inline = "c", group = gD)
c3 = input.color(#1B7F4E, "3rd", inline = "c", group = gD)
cX = input.color(#7A8290, "4th+", inline = "c", group = gD)
lnW = input.int(1, "Line width", minval = 1, maxval = 4, group = gD)
lblSz = input.string("Small", "Label size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = gD)
lblFmt = input.string("1st Break", "Label", options = ["1st Break", "1st Break + price", "1st", "1"], group = gD, tooltip = "\"1st Break + price\" puts the level's price in the label. Useful when a number looks wrong — it says exactly which level took that slot.")

// ===================== ENTRY =================================================
gE = "Entry"
entOn = input.bool(true, "Mark the entry", group = gE, tooltip = "The signal is made the moment the candle that makes the Nth break CLOSES. The marker is placed on the NEXT candle — the one actually taken.")
entAt = input.int(2, "…on which break", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = gE, tooltip = "2 by default: the entry is on the second break.")
entShift = input.int(1, "Marker sits N candles after the break candle", minval = 0, maxval = 10, group = gE)
entTxtBuy = input.string("E: Long", "Buy label", inline = "et", group = gE)
entTxtSell = input.string("E: Short", "Sell label", inline = "et", group = gE)
entShape = input.string("Triangle", "Marker", options = ["Triangle", "Circle", "Arrow", "Diamond"], group = gE)
entSz = input.string("Normal", "Marker size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"], group = gE)
entTxtSz = input.string("Normal", "Label size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"], group = gE)
entBuyC = input.color(#00BF71, "Buy", inline = "ec", group = gE)
entSellC = input.color(#FF4F87, "Sell", inline = "ec", group = gE)
entPad = input.float(0.35, "Gap from the entry level (× ATR)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.05, group = gE)

// ===================== ZONE ==================================================
gZ = "Demand / supply zone"
zoneOn = input.bool(true, "Draw the zone on the 1st break", group = gZ, tooltip = "Drawn at the 1st Break, which is the moment both edges are known.\n\nDEMAND (buy side): top is the 1st Break level, bottom is the low the rally came off.\nSUPPLY (sell side): the mirror — bottom is the 1st Break level, top is the high the decline came off.")
zone50 = input.bool(true, "Mark the 50%", group = gZ)
zoneTxtB = input.string("Demand Zone 50%", "Demand label", group = gZ)
zoneTxtS = input.string("Supply Zone 50%", "Supply label", group = gZ)
zoneExt = input.int(120, "Extend N bars forward", minval = 5, maxval = 400, group = gZ, tooltip = "A fixed width. Boxes that run on indefinitely eventually put a coordinate outside what TradingView will draw.")
zoneBuyC = input.color(#3E7BD6, "Demand", inline = "zc", group = gZ)
zoneSellC = input.color(#D6553E, "Supply", inline = "zc", group = gZ)
zoneFade = input.int(90, "Fill transparency", minval = 0, maxval = 100, group = gZ)
zoneKeep = input.int(2, "Show at most N ACTIVE zones", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = gZ, tooltip = "Only live zones are on the chart, newest kept. 2 by default.")
zoneKill = input.bool(true, "Remove a zone once it is invalidated", group = gZ, tooltip = "A demand zone dies the moment price CLOSES below its bottom edge — the same level the sequence is abandoned under. Supply dies on a close above its top. Dead zones come straight off the chart instead of stacking up behind price.")

// ===================== HELPERS ===============================================
f_size(string s) =>
    s == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : s == "Small" ? size.small : s == "Normal" ? size.normal : s == "Huge" ? size.huge : size.large

f_eshape(string sh, bool up) =>
    sh == "Circle" ? label.style_circle : sh == "Diamond" ? label.style_diamond : sh == "Arrow" ? (up ? label.style_arrowup : label.style_arrowdown) : (up ? label.style_triangleup : label.style_triangledown)

f_ord(int n) =>
    int r100 = n % 100
    int r10 = n % 10
    string sfx = r100 >= 11 and r100 <= 13 ? "th" : r10 == 1 ? "st" : r10 == 2 ? "nd" : r10 == 3 ? "rd" : "th"
    str.tostring(n) + sfx

f_txt(int n, float px) =>
    lblFmt == "1st Break" ? f_ord(n) + " Break" : lblFmt == "1st Break + price" ? f_ord(n) + " Break  " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(px)) : lblFmt == "1st" ? f_ord(n) : str.tostring(n)

f_col(int n) =>
    n == 1 ? c1 : n == 2 ? c2 : n == 3 ? c3 : cX

// TradingView will not accept a drawing coordinate more than ~10,000 bars back.
f_xc(int x) =>
    math.max(x, bar_index - 4000)

// Index of the NEWEST level in `a` that this bar's close is beyond, or -1.
// Newest is the last element, so the scan walks backwards from there.
f_newest(array<float> a, bool up) =>
    int k = -1
    int n = array.size(a)
    if n > 0
        for j = 0 to n - 1
            int i = n - 1 - j
            if k == -1 and (up ? close > array.get(a, i) : close < array.get(a, i))
                k := i
    k

// ===================== STATE =================================================
// Live pools: every confirmed pivot nothing has closed beyond yet.
var array<float> hiP = array.new<float>()
var array<int> hiB = array.new<int>()
var array<float> loP = array.new<float>()
var array<int> loB = array.new<int>()

// The frozen set a running sequence is eating. Taken from the live pool at the
// 1st Break and never added to afterwards.
var array<float> upP = array.new<float>()
var array<int> upB = array.new<int>()
var array<float> dnP = array.new<float>()
var array<int> dnB = array.new<int>()

var bool upOn = false
var bool dnOn = false
var int nUp = 0
var int nDn = 0
var float upFloor = na
var float dnCeil = na
var int upFloorB = na
var int dnCeilB = na

// The low the rally is coming off, and the high the decline is coming off.
// Reset on each new pivot in the same direction, so at the moment a sequence
// freezes these hold the extreme of the leg that just ended. Reading these from
// the pivot pools instead was the bug: the opposite side empties those pools as
// it eats them, so the value was often na and the sequence never got abandoned.
var float rLow = na
var float rHigh = na
var int rLowB = na
var int rHighB = na

var array<line> dLn = array.new<line>()
var array<label> dLb = array.new<label>()
var array<label> eLb = array.new<label>()
var array<box> zBx = array.new<box>()
var array<line> zLn = array.new<line>()
var array<label> zLb = array.new<label>()
// the price that kills each zone, and which way it has to be crossed
var array<float> zKill = array.new<float>()
var array<bool> zBuy = array.new<bool>()

float atr14 = ta.atr(14)

// ===================== TURNING POINTS ========================================
// BODIES, NOT WICKS. The pair sits at offsets [pvLen + 1] (the first candle) and
// [pvLen] (the second); pvLen bars either side of the pair have to stay inside
// it. ta.highest / ta.lowest carry those two windows so there is no variable-
// offset loop: `hiRight` is the highest body top over offsets 0..pvLen-1, and
// the same series read pvLen+2 bars back is the window on the other side.
float bodyHi = math.max(open, close)
float bodyLo = math.min(open, close)
bool cUp = close > open
bool cDn = close < open

float hiRight = ta.highest(bodyHi, pvLen)
float loRight = ta.lowest(bodyLo, pvLen)
float hiLeft = hiRight[pvLen + 2]
float loLeft = loRight[pvLen + 2]

// the body extreme of the pair, and the bar of the two that actually holds it
float pairHi = math.max(bodyHi[pvLen + 1], bodyHi[pvLen])
float pairLo = math.min(bodyLo[pvLen + 1], bodyLo[pvLen])
int pairHiB = bodyHi[pvLen + 1] >= bodyHi[pvLen] ? bar_index - pvLen - 1 : bar_index - pvLen
int pairLoB = bodyLo[pvLen + 1] <= bodyLo[pvLen] ? bar_index - pvLen - 1 : bar_index - pvLen

// bullish handing over to bearish, topping both windows — and the mirror
bool okHi = cUp[pvLen + 1] and cDn[pvLen] and not na(hiLeft) and not na(hiRight) and pairHi > hiLeft and pairHi > hiRight
bool okLo = cDn[pvLen + 1] and cUp[pvLen] and not na(loLeft) and not na(loRight) and pairLo < loLeft and pairLo < loRight

float rawPh = okHi ? pairHi : na
float rawPl = okLo ? pairLo : na
int rawPhB = pairHiB
int rawPlB = pairLoB

if na(rLow) or low < rLow
    rLow := low
    rLowB := bar_index
if na(rHigh) or high > rHigh
    rHigh := high
    rHighB := bar_index

f_mark(int n, float p, int b, bool up) =>
    if showAll or n <= showN
        color col = f_col(n)
        array.push(dLn, line.new(f_xc(b), p, bar_index, p, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = col, width = lnW))
        array.push(dLb, label.new(int(math.avg(f_xc(b), bar_index)), p, f_txt(n, p), xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none, textcolor = col, size = f_size(lblSz)))
        while array.size(dLn) > 480
            line.delete(array.shift(dLn))
        while array.size(dLb) > 480
            label.delete(array.shift(dLb))
    array.size(dLn)

// The break candle has CLOSED — that is the signal. The marker goes on the next
// candle, the one taken. Two labels so the text is plain coloured type rather
// than a filled block.
//
// It is anchored to the break candle's CLOSE, which is the entry level itself.
// Hanging it off the candle's low instead is what threw it so far away: on a
// wide break candle the low can sit a long way under the price you are actually
// getting in at, and the marker went down there with it.
f_entry(bool isBuy) =>
    float pad = atr14 * entPad
    color col = isBuy ? entBuyC : entSellC
    int x = bar_index + entShift
    float y = isBuy ? close - pad : close + pad
    array.push(eLb, label.new(x, y, "", xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = f_eshape(entShape, isBuy), color = col, textcolor = col, size = f_size(entSz)))
    array.push(eLb, label.new(x, isBuy ? y - pad * 1.4 : y + pad * 1.4, isBuy ? entTxtBuy : entTxtSell, xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none, textcolor = col, size = f_size(entTxtSz)))
    while array.size(eLb) > 200
        label.delete(array.shift(eLb))
    array.size(eLb)

// Drawn at the 1st Break: the far edge is that level, the near edge is the
// extreme the move came off. `lvl` is the 1st Break level, `ext` the extreme.
f_zone(float lvl, float ext, int fromB, bool isBuy) =>
    if zoneOn and not na(ext) and not na(fromB)
        float top = isBuy ? lvl : ext
        float bot = isBuy ? ext : lvl
        if top > bot
            color col = isBuy ? zoneBuyC : zoneSellC
            int x1 = f_xc(fromB)
            int x2 = bar_index + zoneExt
            float mid = math.avg(top, bot)
            array.push(zBx, box.new(x1, top, x2, bot, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(col, 40), bgcolor = color.new(col, zoneFade)))
            array.push(zLn, zone50 ? line.new(x1, mid, x2, mid, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(col, 20), style = line.style_dashed) : line.new(x1, mid, x1, mid, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(col, 100)))
            array.push(zLb, label.new(int(math.avg(x1, x2)), mid, zone50 ? (isBuy ? zoneTxtB : zoneTxtS) : "", xloc = xloc.bar_index, yloc = yloc.price, style = label.style_none, textcolor = color.new(col, 0), size = size.small))
            array.push(zKill, isBuy ? bot : top)
            array.push(zBuy, isBuy)
            while array.size(zBx) > zoneKeep
                box.delete(array.shift(zBx))
                line.delete(array.shift(zLn))
                label.delete(array.shift(zLb))
                array.shift(zKill)
                array.shift(zBuy)
    array.size(zBx)

// ===================== BUILD THE LIVE POOLS ==================================
// LOWER HIGHS. The pool is a strictly DESCENDING run: a high that a later,
// higher high supersedes was never a lower high in that run, so it leaves.
// Collecting every pivot high regardless is what let a superseded level sit in
// the middle of the sequence and take a number that belongs to the one above it.
if not na(rawPh)
    while array.size(hiP) > 0 and array.get(hiP, array.size(hiP) - 1) <= rawPh
        array.pop(hiP)
        array.pop(hiB)
    int topI = array.size(hiP) - 1
    if topI >= 0 and minGap > 0 and (array.get(hiP, topI) - rawPh) < minGap * atr14
        array.set(hiP, topI, rawPh)
        array.set(hiB, topI, rawPhB)
    else
        array.push(hiP, rawPh)
        array.push(hiB, rawPhB)
    rLow := low
    rLowB := bar_index
    while array.size(hiP) > poolMax
        array.shift(hiP)
        array.shift(hiB)
// HIGHER LOWS — the mirror.
if not na(rawPl)
    while array.size(loP) > 0 and array.get(loP, array.size(loP) - 1) >= rawPl
        array.pop(loP)
        array.pop(loB)
    int topJ = array.size(loP) - 1
    if topJ >= 0 and minGap > 0 and (rawPl - array.get(loP, topJ)) < minGap * atr14
        array.set(loP, topJ, rawPl)
        array.set(loB, topJ, rawPlB)
    else
        array.push(loP, rawPl)
        array.push(loB, rawPlB)
    rHigh := high
    rHighB := bar_index
    while array.size(loP) > poolMax
        array.shift(loP)
        array.shift(loB)

bool fired = false
int lastNo = 0
float lastLvl = na
bool lastUp = false
bool entBuy = false
bool entSell = false

// ===================== BUY SIDE ==============================================
if barstate.isconfirmed and buyOn
    // The setup is done if price closes back under the low the rally came off.
    // The levels that were left in it were NEVER BROKEN, so they go back into
    // the pool, oldest first, ahead of anything newer. Destroying them here is
    // what made the 3rd, 4th, 5th and 6th disappear: a premature sequence
    // earlier in the leg had frozen them, and abandoning it deleted them.
    if upOn and not na(upFloor) and close < upFloor
        upOn := false
        nUp := 0
        while array.size(upP) > 0
            int lastI = array.size(upP) - 1
            array.insert(hiP, 0, array.get(upP, lastI))
            array.insert(hiB, 0, array.get(upB, lastI))
            array.pop(upP)
            array.pop(upB)
        while array.size(hiP) > poolMax
            array.shift(hiP)
            array.shift(hiB)

    // the 1st Break freezes the set as it stands
    if not upOn and f_newest(hiP, true) >= 0
        while array.size(upP) > 0
            array.pop(upP)
            array.pop(upB)
        if array.size(hiP) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(hiP) - 1
                array.push(upP, array.get(hiP, i))
                array.push(upB, array.get(hiB, i))
        while array.size(hiP) > 0
            array.shift(hiP)
            array.shift(hiB)
        upFloor := rLow
        upFloorB := rLowB
        upOn := true
        nUp := 0

    if upOn
        int k = f_newest(upP, true)
        while k >= 0
            float p = array.get(upP, k)
            int b = array.get(upB, k)
            array.remove(upP, k)
            array.remove(upB, k)
            nUp := nUp + 1
            fired := true
            lastNo := nUp
            lastLvl := p
            lastUp := true
            f_mark(nUp, p, b, true)
            if nUp == 1
                f_zone(p, upFloor, upFloorB, true)
            if nUp == entAt
                entBuy := true
                if entOn
                    f_entry(true)
            k := f_newest(upP, true)
        if array.size(upP) == 0
            upOn := false
            nUp := 0

// ===================== SELL SIDE =============================================
if barstate.isconfirmed and sellOn
    if dnOn and not na(dnCeil) and close > dnCeil
        dnOn := false
        nDn := 0
        while array.size(dnP) > 0
            int lastI = array.size(dnP) - 1
            array.insert(loP, 0, array.get(dnP, lastI))
            array.insert(loB, 0, array.get(dnB, lastI))
            array.pop(dnP)
            array.pop(dnB)
        while array.size(loP) > poolMax
            array.shift(loP)
            array.shift(loB)

    if not dnOn and f_newest(loP, false) >= 0
        while array.size(dnP) > 0
            array.pop(dnP)
            array.pop(dnB)
        if array.size(loP) > 0
            for i = 0 to array.size(loP) - 1
                array.push(dnP, array.get(loP, i))
                array.push(dnB, array.get(loB, i))
        while array.size(loP) > 0
            array.shift(loP)
            array.shift(loB)
        dnCeil := rHigh
        dnCeilB := rHighB
        dnOn := true
        nDn := 0

    if dnOn
        int k = f_newest(dnP, false)
        while k >= 0
            float p = array.get(dnP, k)
            int b = array.get(dnB, k)
            array.remove(dnP, k)
            array.remove(dnB, k)
            nDn := nDn + 1
            fired := true
            lastNo := nDn
            lastLvl := p
            lastUp := false
            f_mark(nDn, p, b, false)
            if nDn == 1
                f_zone(p, dnCeil, dnCeilB, false)
            if nDn == entAt
                entSell := true
                if entOn
                    f_entry(false)
            k := f_newest(dnP, false)
        if array.size(dnP) == 0
            dnOn := false
            nDn := 0

// ===================== RETIRE DEAD ZONES =====================================
// A demand zone is finished the moment price CLOSES below its bottom edge, and
// supply the moment price closes above its top. Walk backwards so removing an
// entry does not shift the ones still to be checked.
if barstate.isconfirmed and zoneKill and array.size(zBx) > 0
    for j = 0 to array.size(zBx) - 1
        int i = array.size(zBx) - 1 - j
        if i < array.size(zBx)
            bool dead = array.get(zBuy, i) ? close < array.get(zKill, i) : close > array.get(zKill, i)
            if dead
                box.delete(array.get(zBx, i))
                line.delete(array.get(zLn, i))
                label.delete(array.get(zLb, i))
                array.remove(zBx, i)
                array.remove(zLn, i)
                array.remove(zLb, i)
                array.remove(zKill, i)
                array.remove(zBuy, i)

// ===================== KEEP THE CHART TO WHAT IS BEING LOOKED AT =============
if barstate.islast and histBars > 0
    while array.size(dLn) > 0 and line.get_x2(array.get(dLn, 0)) < bar_index - histBars
        line.delete(array.shift(dLn))
    while array.size(dLb) > 0 and label.get_x(array.get(dLb, 0)) < bar_index - histBars
        label.delete(array.shift(dLb))
    while array.size(eLb) > 0 and label.get_x(array.get(eLb, 0)) < bar_index - histBars
        label.delete(array.shift(eLb))

// ===================== ALERTS ================================================
alertcondition(fired, "Any break", "Basic Breaks — a level was broken")
alertcondition(entBuy, "BUY entry", "Basic Breaks — BUY: the break candle has closed, enter on the next candle")
alertcondition(entSell, "SELL entry", "Basic Breaks — SELL: the break candle has closed, enter on the next candle")
if fired
    alert(f_ord(lastNo) + " Break — " + (lastUp ? "high" : "low") + " @ " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(lastLvl)), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if entBuy or entSell
    alert((entBuy ? "BUY" : "SELL") + " — " + f_ord(entAt) + " break has closed, enter on the next candle", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
